# Sandscape Game

This is a game project managed by the **Sandscape CLI**. Use the
`sandscape-cli` skill (installed globally or under `.claude/skills/`) for the
full workflow — it covers auth, pull/push, import, and publish.

**Before doing anything**, check whether this project is connected to Sandscape:

    test -f .sandscape/project.json && echo "CONNECTED" || echo "NOT CONNECTED"

- **CONNECTED** → run `sandscape pull`, then edit, then `sandscape push`.
- **NOT CONNECTED** → the game is local-only. Run `sandscape init .` to import
  it as a new project on Sandscape (free, requires login).

## Layout

`index.html` at the root is the served entry point. Everything else is your
game — any structure works. `.sandscape/`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`,
`.claude/`, `.agents/` are CLI-managed and never uploaded.

If `.sandscape/design.json` exists, it contains the game's design context
(concept, style, assets). Read it to understand the project.

## AGENTS.md

`AGENTS.md` mirrors this file so agent tooling that looks for either name finds
the same guide. On POSIX it is a symlink to `CLAUDE.md`; on platforms where
symlink creation is not permitted it is written as a small pointer file.
